menu "Sprout feature modules"

# Secure by default: a care view turns on a camera in a child's room, so the
# capability stays off until the product enables it for the profile AND a
# guardian has explicitly turned it on in the parent app. The device additionally
# refuses to start unless it can show a visible and audible indication.
config FEATURE_CARE_VIEW
    bool "Enable guardian live camera view"
    default n
    depends on FEATURE_CAMERA_CAPTURE && FEATURE_SCREEN_SURFACE && FEATURE_AUDIO_OUTPUT && FEATURE_PROMPT_TONE && FEATURE_BUTTON_INPUT && FEATURE_DEVICE_MESSAGE && FEATURE_DEVICE_IDENTITY
    help
        Lets a guardian open a short live view of the device camera from the
        parent app. The device shows an on-screen notice and plays a prompt when
        a view starts, refuses to start if either is unavailable, stops the view
        when the child presses the button, and enforces the session deadline on
        its own instead of trusting the platform. Frames are sent over the relay
        and are never written to flash, the SD card, or the logs.

config CARE_VIEW_MAX_SECONDS
    int "Longest single care view, in seconds"
    depends on FEATURE_CARE_VIEW
    range 30 300
    default 180
    help
        Hard upper bound the device enforces regardless of what the platform
        asks for. A camera left running in a child's room is the failure mode
        this limit exists to prevent.

config CARE_VIEW_FRAME_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Milliseconds between captured frames"
    depends on FEATURE_CARE_VIEW
    range 200 5000
    default 500
    help
        Lower values give a smoother view at the cost of bandwidth and power. The
        relay may serve a slower rate than this, never a faster one.

config CARE_VIEW_MAX_FRAME_BYTES
    int "Largest single frame in bytes"
    depends on FEATURE_CARE_VIEW
    range 8192 262144
    default 131072
    help
        A frame larger than this is dropped rather than sent, so one bad capture
        cannot stall the uplink or exhaust memory.

config CARE_VIEW_MAX_SESSION_SECONDS
    int "Longest accepted session, in seconds"
    depends on FEATURE_CARE_VIEW
    range 30 300
    default 180
    help
        A session whose deadline is further out than this is clamped, so the
        platform cannot extend a view beyond the device's own policy.

endmenu
